Scope: crates/bbt-mux/** except identity implementation; app main.rs four-line early mcp dispatch; no dependency or Cargo.lock edit.
Acceptance 1: installed clients use the compiled app MCP stdio entry, call orient, say Executor, and produce signed seat/{id}/control audits with correct seat and generation. See interop-02 and final interop-03 logs. Raw client output is inspected only in memory and discarded. No real task/transcript export.
Protocol: initialize, ping, tools/list, tools/call only; bounded newline JSON-RPC. Optional params._meta["bboxy450/op_id"] preserves an explicit nonce; otherwise minted once per call. No automatic transport retry; unknown response retains nonce.
Authority: logic admission + supervisor-confirmed generation + current local issuer policy/class/epoch. Workers cannot claim actor/operator fields, cross-swarm reads or Oracle execution graphs. Cached results require identical actor/tool/args. Current local-dev provider remains explicit, not a GPG-chain claim.
Results/audit: one seat SQLite transaction stores the first read result plus audit intent. Retry returns that result; replay audit signed and event-ID-deduplicated. Failure injection checks rollback; reopen checks retained result; concurrent retry checks one dispatch. Audit preserves insertion order, stores argument digest and no argument payload.
Read projections: five tools, bounded own briefs/channel tree/execution context, metadata and in-memory graphs. unread_count=null with reason; pending_application_ack is separate and checked before/after recipient ack.

